  "summary": "September bonfires crowned with daisies: Ethiopia's demera pyres mark the Finding of the True Cross.",
  "description": "Meskel (September 26-27) builds demera — huge pyres of branches and stakes crowned with yellow Meskel daisies and crossed with ox-tail whisks — in every town square. Priests in velvet and gold circle the pyre with drums and prayer, the torch is lit, and the direction the towering cone collapses is read as blessing for the year. The feast commemorates Empress Helena's finding of the True Cross by smoke-vision, and UNESCO lists the celebration as intangible heritage; Addis Ababa's Meskel Square holds hundreds of thousands.",
